    "We chose not to drop the 52 rows with missing nutritional values because:\n",
    "\n",
    "- 5.5% is small but not negligible: losing these rows would remove real signal from the model\n",
    "- 39 of them are high-traffic: dropping them would underrepresent the positive class, which is critical for predicting popular recipes\n",
    "\n",
    "For imputation, we'll use the **median per category** rather than the global median, as recipes in the same category likely share similar nutritional profiles. All categories with missing values have enough non-missing rows to compute a reliable median. The nutritional columns were confirmed to be non-normally distributed further supporting the use of median. The table below shows the median values used for imputation:"
