   "source": [
    "## Model Fitting & Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "Predicting high-traffic recipes is a **binary classification problem** in machine learning. We chose **Logistic Regression** as the primary model because it is well-suited for binary outcomes, provides interpretable coefficients, and serves as a strong baseline for classification tasks. The comparison model I am choosing is a **Decision Tree classifier**, chosen for its interpretability and ability to handle non-linear relationships.\n",
    "\n",
    "For evaluation, we use three metrics: **Accuracy**, **Precision**, and **Recall**. Accuracy measures the overall proportion of correctly classified recipes. Recall measures how many of the truly popular recipes the model successfully identifies. **Precision is the key business metric** here -- it measures how many of the recipes predicted as high-traffic are actually high-traffic, directly addressing the goal of correctly identifying popular recipes 80% of the time."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
